  "Five published descriptive numbers did not reproduce and are not used as checks: the SD of age of the musicians (paper 8.76, rows 8.77), the SDs of the non-musicians' years of playing (0.76 vs 0.77) and of lessons (0.77 vs 0.78), and the musicians' mean (5.77 vs 5.79) and SD (0.42 vs 0.43) of the importance of music (one musician has no answer in the deposit). The paper rates importance on a 7-point scale from 1 to 7 while the codebook says 0 to 6.",
